.TH FLUXLAND-STARTUP 5 "2026-10-25" "fluxland 2.0.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
fluxland-startup \- autostart script for fluxland
.SH DESCRIPTION
The startup file is a shell script executed when
.BR fluxland (1)
starts.
It is used to launch applications, set wallpapers, configure displays,
or perform other initialization tasks.
.PP
By default, the file is located at
.I ~/.config/fluxland/startup
within the configuration directory.
.SH EXECUTION
The startup script runs after the compositor is fully initialized and
the Wayland socket is available.
The
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
environment variable is set before the script executes.
.PP
If the startup file has the executable permission bit set
.RB ( "chmod +x" ),
it is executed directly.
Otherwise, it is run via
.BR /bin/sh .
.PP
The script is launched using a double-fork mechanism: the compositor
does not wait for the script to exit and does not manage its child
processes.
Long-running programs started from the script are inherited by the
init process.
.PP
When fluxland reads a Fluxbox directory itself
.RI ( ~/.fluxbox ,
having none of its own), its
.I startup
runs as
.B fluxland \-\-import\-fluxbox
would make it: up to its
.B exec fluxbox
(which would start Fluxbox on Xwayland), with the programs that only work
on an X display commented out, each with the reason.
That copy is written to
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fluxland\-fluxbox\-startup ;
what it leaves out is logged.
.PP
In addition to the startup file, a command can be passed via the
.B \-s
option on the
.BR fluxland (1)
command line.
Both the startup file and the
.B \-s
command are executed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The following environment variables are available to the startup script:
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The name of the Wayland socket (e.g.\&
.IR wayland-0 ).
.TP
.B FLUXLAND_SOCK
Path to the IPC socket for
.BR fluxland-ctl (1).
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Xwayland's display, for X11 programs (Xwayland starts when the first
one connects).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The XDG runtime directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
The desktop is fluxland's to draw (the style's
.BR background ,
or the
.B SetWallpaper
command) and outputs are set in the init
.RB ( session.output.* );
the script starts programs:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
#!/bin/sh
# Notifications, a panel and a terminal
mako &
waybar &
foot &

# Lock the screen after ten minutes
swayidle -w timeout 600 'swaylock -f' &
.fi
.RE
.PP
Make the script executable:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
chmod +x ~/.config/fluxland/startup
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fluxland/startup
Default startup script location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fluxland (1),
.BR fluxland-init (5)
